---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Reviews from "../../components/Reviews.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Commercial Lock Rekeying in Delaware | 1st Capital Locksmith"
  description="Professional commercial lock rekeying in Delaware, fast and affordable, no disruption to business. Call (302) 735-0050."
>

  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="bg-white border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-3">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 flex-wrap">
        <li>
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Home</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <a href="/services/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Services</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <span class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold">Commercial Lock Rekeying</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Schema: Breadcrumbs -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://1stcapitallocksmithde.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://1stcapitallocksmithde.com/services/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Commercial Lock Rekeying", "item": "https://1stcapitallocksmithde.com/services/commercial-lock-rekeying/" }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: Service -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Commercial Lock Rekeying in Delaware",
    "description": "Professional commercial lock rekeying for offices, retail stores, warehouses, medical facilities, and multi-tenant commercial properties throughout Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith rekeyes existing locks to new keys without full replacement, restoring access control quickly and affordably.",
    "provider": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "1st Capital Locksmith",
      "telephone": "+13027350050",
      "address": { "@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "2089 S Dupont Hwy #2", "addressLocality": "Dover", "addressRegion": "DE", "postalCode": "19901", "addressCountry": "US" },
      "geo": { "@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": "39.1212111", "longitude": "-75.5331705" }
    },
    "areaServed": {
      "@type": "State",
      "name": "Delaware"
    },
    "serviceType": "Commercial Lock Rekeying"
  })} />


  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative min-h-85 md:min-h-125 flex items-center text-white py-10 md:py-20"
    style="background-image: url('/images/commercial-lock-rekeying.png'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/72"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-6 z-10">
      <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-xs md:text-sm mb-2 md:mb-4">Commercial Lock Rekeying — Delaware</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-3 md:mb-6 max-w-3xl leading-tight">
        Commercial Lock Rekeying in Delaware — Protect Your Business Without Replacing Your Locks
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm md:text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-5 md:mb-8">
        Employee terminated? Lost a master key? Moving into a new commercial space? 1st Capital Locksmith provides professional commercial lock rekeying for offices, retail stores, warehouses, and multi-tenant buildings throughout Delaware — quickly, affordably, and with minimal disruption to your operations.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <a
          href="tel:3027350050"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-bold text-base md:text-lg hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
        >
          Call (302) 735-0050
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact/"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-white px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-semibold text-sm md:text-base hover:bg-white hover:text-[#1A1F22] transition"
        >
          Get a Free Quote
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Bar -->
  <section class="bg-[#0E1B2F] py-8">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">All Commercial Locks</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Offices, Retail, Warehouses & More</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">No Lock Replacement</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Rekey Existing Hardware — Save Money</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Master Key Systems</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Designed & Implemented On-Site</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">After-Hours Available</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Minimal Disruption to Your Business</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Delaware's Commercial Rekeying Experts</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6 leading-snug">
            Commercial Lock Rekeying Service Throughout Delaware
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Key control is one of the most overlooked security vulnerabilities in commercial properties. When employees leave — whether voluntarily or not — when keys go missing, when you move into a previously occupied space, or when you simply don't know who has copies of your business keys, you have a real security gap. Rekeying is the fastest, most cost-effective way to close that gap.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Commercial lock rekeying reconfigures the internal pin stack of your existing lock cylinders so that all previously issued keys no longer operate the lock, and new keys do. The lock hardware itself stays in place — no new holes, no new hardware, no costly installation labor. It's the same result as replacing every lock on your property, at a fraction of the cost.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            1st Capital Locksmith provides professional commercial lock rekeying throughout Delaware for all types of businesses — offices, retail stores, restaurants, medical facilities, warehouses, storage facilities, and multi-tenant commercial buildings. We work efficiently to minimize any disruption to your operations and can schedule after-hours service when needed. We serve Dover, Milford, Smyrna, Camden, Harrington, and all of Kent County, Delaware.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Photo Slot 1 -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-[#F8F8F5] aspect-[4/3] flex items-center justify-center">
            <img
              src="/images/commercial-lock-rekeying-service.png"
              alt="Professional commercial lock rekeying service in Delaware"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
              width="600"
              height="450"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6">When Your Business Needs Rekeying:</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {[
                "Employee Terminated or Resigned",
                "Lost or Unaccounted-For Master Key",
                "Moving Into New Commercial Space",
                "New Ownership or Management Change",
                "Contractor or Vendor Key Not Returned",
                "Security Audit or Policy Upgrade",
                "Break-In or Attempted Entry",
                "Tenant Turnover in Commercial Building",
                "Keys Duplicated Without Authorization",
                "Don't Know Who Has Copies of Your Keys",
              ].map((item) => (
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-700">
                  <span class="w-6 h-6 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3">
                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  {item}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
              <a
                href="tel:3027350050"
                class="w-full inline-flex justify-center items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 text-white font-bold hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
              >
                Call (302) 735-0050 Now
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">What We Rekey</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">
          Commercial Lock Rekeying Services in Delaware
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          We rekey all common commercial lock types for every kind of business across Delaware. Here's a breakdown of the commercial rekeying situations we handle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8">

        <!-- Office Building Rekeying -->
        <div id="office-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 21V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v16m14 0h2m-2 0h-5m-9 0H3m2 0h5M9 7h1m-1 4h1m4-4h1m-1 4h1m-5 10v-5a1 1 0 011-1h2a1 1 0 011 1v5m-4 0h4" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Office Building Lock Rekeying in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Office buildings present a complex key control challenge. Over time — through employee turnover, contractor access, cleaning crews, temporary staff, and key duplication — the number of people who have had access to your office keys can grow well beyond what you're aware of. A single disgruntled former employee with a retained key represents a significant security liability.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith rekeyes office building locks throughout Delaware, from single-suite offices to multi-floor commercial buildings. We work methodically through each entry point — front door, suite doors, server rooms, executive offices, storage rooms, and any other keyed access points — rekeying each cylinder and issuing a fresh, controlled set of keys with a clear key record.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We can also set up or refine a <a href="/services/master-key-systems/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key system</a> during the rekeying process, so you have tiered access — a master key for ownership or management that opens everything, and departmental or individual keys that only open the doors each person needs. This is best practice for professional office security and an upgrade that costs very little to implement when done at the time of rekeying.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Retail Store Rekeying -->
        <div id="retail-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16 11V7a4 4 0 00-8 0v4M5 9h14l1 12H4L5 9z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Retail Store Lock Rekeying in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Retail environments have some of the highest key turnover of any business type. High staff turnover, seasonal employees, shift managers with after-hours access, and delivery personnel with back-door keys all contribute to a key control situation that can quickly become unmanageable. Rekeying at regular intervals — or immediately when key control is compromised — is essential.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              We rekey retail store locks throughout Delaware quickly and efficiently, typically scheduling service during opening or closing hours so your day of business is unaffected. We rekey front entry locks, back-of-house doors, storage room locks, office locks, and any other keyed access points on your retail property.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              For retailers with multiple locations in Delaware, we can coordinate rekeying across all sites on a single schedule, issuing a consistent key control system across your entire operation. Call (302) 735-0050 to discuss a rekeying plan for your retail business.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Warehouse & Industrial Rekeying -->
        <div id="warehouse-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 14v3m4-3v3m4-3v3M3 21h18M3 10h18M3 7l9-4 9 4M4 10h16v11H4V10z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Warehouse & Industrial Lock Rekeying in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Warehouses, distribution centers, manufacturing facilities, and industrial properties face unique security requirements. Multiple entry points, loading dock access, secured inventory areas, equipment storage, and shift-based workforce management all require a thoughtful key control approach. When a key goes missing or an employee with after-hours access leaves, the security exposure is significant.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith provides commercial rekeying for warehouse and industrial properties throughout Delaware. We work with facility managers to inventory all lock cylinders, establish a rekeying plan, and execute efficiently — often during non-operational hours or shift changes to avoid disruption. We handle heavy-duty commercial locks, padlocks, and access-control-integrated cylinders commonly found in industrial settings.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We can also implement a <a href="/services/master-key-systems/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key hierarchy</a> appropriate for your facility — with ownership-level masters, shift supervisor keys, and restricted individual access keys — all rekeyed from your existing lock hardware.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- After Employee Termination -->
        <div id="employee-termination" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18.364 18.364A9 9 0 005.636 5.636m12.728 12.728A9 9 0 015.636 5.636m12.728 12.728L5.636 5.636" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Emergency Commercial Rekeying After Employee Termination in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              When an employee is terminated — especially under difficult circumstances — immediate rekeying of your facility is not optional, it's essential. A former employee who retains key access, or who made copies of their business keys, is a serious threat to your property, inventory, and data. Businesses that wait to rekey after a termination take on substantial risk.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith provides same-day commercial rekeying throughout Delaware for post-termination situations. We understand the urgency — call us and we'll prioritize getting a locksmith to your business as quickly as possible. We rekey all affected cylinders and provide a fresh set of keys only to authorized personnel.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Proactive businesses also schedule a periodic rekeying review — typically annually — to audit key control and reset access regardless of specific incidents. This is best practice for any commercial property that issues keys to employees. Ask us about setting up a recurring rekeying schedule for your Delaware business.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Master Key System Rekeying -->
        <div id="master-key-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 7a2 2 0 012 2m4 0a6 6 0 01-7.743 5.743L11 17H9v2H7v2H4a1 1 0 01-1-1v-2.586a1 1 0 01.293-.707l5.964-5.964A6 6 0 1121 9z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Commercial Master Key System Rekeying in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A master key system allows one key (the master) to open all locks in a facility, while individual sub-keys only open specific designated doors. This is the standard for professional commercial security — it means a manager doesn't need to carry a full ring of keys, while individual employees only have access to what they need. When a master key is lost or compromised, the entire system must be rekeyed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith designs and rekeyes master key systems for commercial properties throughout Delaware. Whether you need to rekey an existing master key system because a master key was lost, or you want to implement a master key system for the first time using your existing lock hardware, we handle the pinning, key cutting, and documentation to set it up correctly.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              A properly implemented master key system significantly simplifies day-to-day key management while maintaining controlled access for all personnel levels. We serve offices, medical practices, property management companies, and multi-tenant commercial buildings throughout Delaware.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Multi-Tenant Commercial Building -->
        <div id="multitenant-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 7v10a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2V9a2 2 0 00-2-2h-6l-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Multi-Tenant Commercial Building Rekeying in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Commercial property managers and building owners who manage multi-tenant properties face a recurring rekeying need at every tenant turnover. Each outgoing tenant has had key access to their suite, building common areas, parking structures, and utility rooms — and depending on how long they've been in the building, may have distributed keys widely among their staff.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith handles commercial tenant turnover rekeying throughout Delaware for property management companies and individual building owners. We rekey suite locks, common area locks, and any other cylinders the outgoing tenant had access to, and we coordinate new key issuance to the incoming tenant before they take possession.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We also help property managers establish and maintain a <a href="/services/master-key-systems/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key system</a> for the building — where the building master opens all suites (for maintenance and emergency access) while tenant sub-masters only open their specific suite. This is the professional standard for commercial building management in Delaware.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- New Commercial Space -->
        <div id="new-space-rekeying" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v6m0 0v6m0-6h6m-6 0H6" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Rekeying a New Commercial Space in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Moving into a new commercial space — whether it's a new lease, a purchased building, or a newly constructed space where contractors had key access — is one of the most important times to rekey. You have no way of knowing how many keys exist from previous tenants, previous owners, or the construction crew, and you have no control over where those keys are or who has them.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Rekeying before or immediately after you move in establishes clean key control from day one. Every key in existence from that moment forward is one that you issued and are tracking. This is the professional standard for any business moving into a commercial space, and it's something we strongly recommend to every business owner we work with.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We work with businesses setting up new locations throughout Delaware, often coordinating with landlords and property managers to ensure the rekeying is done at the right time in the move-in process. Call (302) 735-0050 before or during your move-in to schedule a rekeying that sets your new space up securely from the start.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Photo Gallery Strip -->
  <section class="bg-white py-14">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src="/images/commercial-lock-rekeying-close-up.jpg"
            alt="Close-up of commercial lock being rekeyed in Delaware"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            width="480"
            height="360"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[#F8F8F5]">
            <p class="font-semibold text-[#1A1F22] text-sm">Commercial Lock Rekeying</p>
            <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-1">Pin-by-pin precision on all commercial lock types</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src="/images/locksmith-rekeying-office-door.jpg"
            alt="Locksmith rekeying office door lock in Delaware"
            class="w-full h-64 object-cover"
            width="480"
            height="360"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-[#F8F8F5]">
            <p class="font-semibold text-[#1A1F22] text-sm">On-Site at Your Business</p>
